  "notes": "{放|はな}つ covers three related ideas: releasing something, firing a projectile, and emitting light or smell. It has a literary or dramatic tone compared to everyday alternatives.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: Xを{放|はな}つ\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{放|はな}っている indicates an ongoing state of emission: {光|ひかり}を{放|はな}っている (is emitting light).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {矢|や}を{放|はな}つ (shoot an arrow)\n- {光|ひかり}を{放|はな}つ (emit light)\n- {香|かお}りを{放|はな}つ (give off a fragrance)\n- {野|の}に{放|はな}つ (release into the wild)\n- {異彩|いさい}を{放|はな}つ (stand out, be distinctive)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {放|はな}す: to release, let go (everyday, physical release)\n- {放|はな}つ: to release, emit (literary, broader range including light/arrows)",
